From 36f5b870f6c44c7ea4bead492d3deb68ba513ac4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 19:30:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Security review 2026-09-12: policy routing failure paths, the
 Advisor's TLS clock, a port gate, certificate scripts, diag 14f

Policy Routing (rc/reaper_pbr.c, rc/rwatch.c):
- a Killswitch or enable toggled INSIDE the commit-confirm window was lost:
  reaper_pbr_regen() stepped aside while armed, Keep promoted the stale
  candidate and the deadline ran a stale recovery. Both are now regenerated
  and the candidate re-run, under a new file_lock("reaper_pbr") that apply
  takes too; token and deadline untouched (R04).
- a WireGuard bypass that cannot be installed (table full, write rejected,
  LAN net unknown) is a counted failure -> exit 2 / E_PARTIAL, named in
  syslog; the "bypass is in place" line is suppressed. It was a log line
  and a clean apply (R05).
- ipset/domain selectors are resolved against the object layer: a group
  expands into its usable members (it never had a set of its own), geo, MAC
  and unknown objects drop the rule with the reason. The page no longer
  offers geo or MAC objects (R06).
- ip rule adds are checked (pbr_route); expect_rules/expect_rules6 are the
  INTENDED counts, per family - the old live-table grep matched a failed
  add's own absence; the v6 half is checked while IPv6 is enabled; rwatch
  heals per family (R07).
Advisor (rmcpd/rmcpd.c): the 20 s request clock is armed before the TLS
wrap - SO_RCVTIMEO bounds one read, not the handshake (R10).
Port forwarding (rc/firewall.c): a space-stripped "80-jACCEPT" passed the
charset gate and was emitted as a malformed --dport, and the nat table is one
atomic restore, so one bad nvram value took MASQUERADE down with it.
_fw_ports_ok() drops and names such a rule (found by the emitter harness
while evaluating the R15 field report, which is not a confirmed defect).
OpenVPN certificates (libovpn/openvpn_setup.c): the generated scripts export
HOME as the key directory - the easy-rsa config points RANDFILE at
$ENV::HOME/.rnd, rc runs with HOME=/, and OpenSSL 3.x exits 1 when it cannot
write that file after the CSR is already on disk, so pkitool's && chain
stopped before openssl ca (field 2026-09-12, R16; the second cause after
this morning's AKID fix).
reaper_diag v1.3.15: section 14f, the port-forwarding truth in one place
(switches, VSERVER hook, chain, every saved rule against the live table)
with findings.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
